Paradroid's changes to Yape (github.com/calmopyrin/yapesdl, at f5fcf8d):
- all of SDL's events each frame, not one (a gamepad's stream of axis
  events left its stick far behind);
- YAPE_PADKEYS=off: the gamepad's buttons do nothing but fire (B stepped
  the active joystick on, LB typed RUN, RB opened the menu);
- for the tests: SIGUSR1 enters the monitor, reading stdin; SIGUSR2 saves
  the TED's picture as a PPM to $YAPE_SHOT ($YAPE_SHOTN of them, one a
  frame); YAPE_WARP starts without the speed limit; YAPE_JOYLOG writes each
  change of the joystick ports as read, with the time.
- the ROMs the settings name are loaded at start-up, not only at the next
  hard reset: a cartridge in yape.conf (Demon Attack's run-yape.sh puts one
  there) starts with the machine.

